ThinkPart(
    type='think',
    think='Structural verification reveals issues (text nodes don\'t auto-size width in auto-layout as I hoped — they keep hug widths and some overflow their parents):\n\n1. **Display text overflows**: "display" tex
t width 1603px inside a 640px hero copy frame — it didn\'t wrap. Text nodes are created with auto-width, so long texts overflow horizontally. Same for "lead" (1274 wide in 640 frame), "body" in ch02 (2751 wide!), qu
ote texts (1191-1225 wide in 410 frames!), bio (2417 in 720), service descs (~500 in 305 cards).\n2. Several frames have white fills where I intended transparent — minor (white on paper bg shows as white boxes; e.g.
, "quiz cards" frame is white fill covering... it\'s inside paper-deep band; it\'ll render as a white strip behind the cards — sloppy). Also "hero plate", "doctor plate", "doctor copy", "quotes", "locations", "cta r
ow", "nav right" frames have default white fills. These create unintended white boxes.\n3. Utility bar facts width 744 centered — fine.\n4. The ghost button label color #e3e9e1 on white fill (button frame has white 
fill!) — "ghost on dark" frame fill white with sage stroke on dark band → renders as white button, not ghost. Need transparent fill.\n5. Fixed heights: hero 720 vs content 528+padding 192 = fits. But the overflowing
texts break the layout visually.\n\nFixes needed:\nA. Resize overflowing text nodes to fixed widths so they wrap: when you resize a text node in Figma, it becomes fixed-size and wraps. I can use resize_node on each 
overflowing text to set width (height auto-adjusts? resize_node sets explicit width/height; for text, setting width with any height should enable wrapping... risk: it sets fixed height too. In Figma API, resize on t
ext sets textAutoResize to NONE? Actually figma.node.resize(w,h) keeps autoResize behavior: if textAutoResize is HEIGHT, resizing width keeps height auto. The plugin\'s resize likely maps to node.resize. Text nodes 
created via bridge probably have textAutoResize "WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT" (auto width). After resize(w,h), Figma sets it to... hmm, node.resize() on a text with autoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT will change autoResize to NONE? L
et me check Figma API: calling resize() on text sets textAutoResize to "NONE" if it was "WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT"? Actually in Figma, textAutoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT means auto width+height; resize() sets the node to fixed
size and textAutoResize becomes "NONE". With NONE, text wraps within fixed width and clips height... it wraps but doesn\'t auto-grow height. If height too small → clipped text. So I should resize with generous heigh
t.\n\nBetter approach: resize each long text node to (desiredWidth, largeHeight)? With NONE auto-resize, extra height just leaves empty space — in auto-layout that adds gaps. Hmm.\n\nAlternative: compute approximate
wrapped heights. fontSize 16, lineHeight ~19.4; text of ~300 chars at width 610 → ~50 chars/line → 6 lines → ~116px. I can estimate conservatively and set height slightly above; auto-layout will have minor extra spa
ce — acceptable.\n\nSimplest robust alternative: delete and recreate text nodes with explicit width... create_text has no width param. So resize is the way. Let me set textAutoResize via resize: first resize to (wid
th, estimated height). Let me estimate per node:\n\n- 5:169 display (54px, lh 65.35): width 620 → chars 61 at avg ~28px/char ≈ 61 chars → wait 61 chars/line? Rough: 54px font, avg char width ~0.5em = 27px → 620/27 ≈
23 chars/line. Text is 61 chars → 3 lines → height ≈ 196. Set 620x210.\n- 5:170 lead (17px, lh 20.6): 150 chars, width 620 → avg char ~8.5px → 72 chars/line → 3 lines → 62. Set 620x70.\n- 5:182 body ch02 (16px, lh 1
9.4): 369 chars, width 1280 → ~80 chars... avg char 8px → 160 chars/line → 3 lines → 58. Set 1280x66.\n- 5:233 bio (15px, lh 18.2): 319 chars, width 720 → ~96 chars/line → 4 lines → 73. Set 720x82.\n- quote texts 5:
242/244/246 (16px, lh 19.4): ~130-140 chars, width 362 (410-48) → ~45 chars/line → 4 lines → 78. Set 362x90.\n- service descs (13px, lh 15.7): ~90 chars, width 257 → ~39 chars/line → 3 lines → 47. Set 257x52. (8 nod
es: 5:204,207,210,213,216,219,222,225)\n- 5:187/189 quiz descs (14px, lh 16.9): ~80 chars, width 572 → ~80 chars/line → 2 lines → 34. Set 572x40.\n- 5:259 hours fees (14px, lh 16.9): 217 chars, width 1280 → ~150 cha
rs/line → 2 lines → 34. Set 1280x40.\n- 5:268 facts col (13px, lh 15.7): 205 chars, width 1280 → ~164/line → 2 lines → 32. Set 1280x36.\n- 5:267 links col: 137 chars → 1-2 lines at 1280 → set 1280x36.\n- 5:248 link,
5:234 link, 5:172 stats, headings: single line, fine as-is (they fit width? 5:237 heading 644 < 1280 ok; 5:192 706 ok; 5:251 794 ok).\n- 5:159 utility facts: 744 wide in 1280 centered — ok.\n- 5:162 nav links 270 ok
.\n\nB. Transparent fills: frames that should be transparent: 5:161 nav right, 5:167 hero plate, 5:171 cta row, 5:183 quiz cards, 5:193 service grid (white on white — ch03 fill is #ffffff? I set ch03 fill... I creat
ed ch03 services without fillColor → default white. Page bg is paper #f7f4ee so ch03 band renders white — that was intended? I alternated: hero white? Hmm. Let me check my design intent: page fill paper. ch01 hero: 
created without fill → white. That\'s wrong vs my design (hero on paper). Actually looking at fills: ch01 = white, ch02 = paper-deep, ch03 = white, ch04 = paper-deep, ch05 = white, ch06 = sage-ink, footer = ink. Hmm
— that gives white chapters vs paper page. My original intent: hero + ch03 + ch05 on paper bg, ch02/ch04 paper-deep, ch06 dark. The white chapters deviate but honestly look fine too (paper page with white bands)... 
no wait, if chapters are full-bleed white, the paper bg never shows except... utility bar is paper-deep, page bg paper shows nowhere except as margins? Page bg shows only if chapter bands don\'t cover full width — t
hey\'re all 1440 wide = full bleed. So the whole page is white/paper-deep/dark bands. The paper bg is invisible. That\'s a flatter look than intended ("warm ivory paper" is Direction A\'s signature!). \n\nDecision: 
make ch01, ch03, ch05 transparent (paper shows through) — that\'s the editorial ivory look. And remove fills on inner group frames (nav right, cta rows, quiz cards row, service grid, hero plate, doctor plate, doctor
copy, quotes row, locations row).\n\nCan I set transparent fill via set_fill_color with a:0? set_fill_color has optional a param. Set a:0.\n\nC. "ghost on dark" 5:262: fill → transparent (a:0). \nD. "secondary" 5:17
6 white fill on paper hero — keep white? Hero on paper; secondary button white is fine.\nE. quote cards fill sage-tint — good.\nF. doctor copy frame white fill — make transparent so paper-deep band shows.\nG. hero p
late frame white — transparent.\n\nAlso heights: after texts wrap to multi-line, parent fixed heights may overflow: hero copy frame height 528 fixed; content: eyebrow 16 + display 210 + lead 70 + cta 52 + stats 17 +
spacing 20×4 = 445 — fits. ch02: 560 total, content: 16+44+66+150 + spacing 24×3 + padding 160 = 508 — fits. Quotes row 280 fixed; quote frame padding 48 + text 90 + attr 15 + spacing 12 = 165 — fits (extra space bo
ttom, fine). Service cards 300 fixed: padding 48 + num 16 + title 23 + desc 52 + spacing 20 = 159 — fits. ch04: doctor copy content ≈ 16+39+82+18+48 spacing = 203 in 480 — fits. ch06: content: 16+44+190+40+52 + spac
ing 24×4 + padding 160 = 598 — fits in 700. Footer: content 22+16+36+15+42 spacing + 96 padding = 227 in 280 — fits.\n\nAlso auto-layout: hero copy frame has fixed height 528 — extra empty space at bottom, ok. But a
ctually — since chapters have fixed heights and inner content hugs, there will be some bottom whitespace in several bands; acceptable for a design file.\n\nOne more: the service grid only used 2 rows of 4? Grid: 128
0 wide, cards 305 + 20 spacing → 4 per row = 1280 exactly (305*4+20*3=1280). 8 cards → 2 rows. Grid height 640 fixed (300*2+20+... = 620 + padding? no padding → 620) fits.\n\nAlso page frame height 9200 fixed: child
ren sum = 36+76+720+560+900+640+620+700+280 = 4532. Page 9200 → half empty. I should resize page frame to ~4550 (auto-layout with fixed height keeps empty space; better set height hug? It\'s a top-level frame; make 
it 4560). Similarly inner frames\' heights are fixed; fine.\n\nLet me also fix the section "05 Desktop" position — page frame is at x=100 within section at (0,2750)? Its absoluteBoundingBox x=100 y=2850 — good, insi
de section (0,2750,1640,9400).\n\nBatch the fixes now:\n1. Transparent fills (a:0) on: 5:154\'s children ch01 5:164, ch03 5:190, ch05 5:235; inner groups 5:161, 5:167, 5:171, 5:183, 5:193, 5:227, 5:228, 5:238, 5:252
, 5:260, 5:262.\n2. Resize text nodes for wrapping.\n3. Resize page frame 5:154 → height 4560. And section 5:7 height is 9400 — fine (contains services page later too).\n\nset_fill_color params: nodeId, r,g,b, a opt
ional. Set a:0 with any rgb.',
    encrypted=None
)
